    <ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>&lt;div&gt;A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 26 November 2020, the Minister of Justice introduced Bill C-13, An Act to amend the Criminal Code (single event sport betting), in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.    &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-13 amends paragraph 207(4)(b) of the Criminal Code to make it lawful for the government of a province or territory, or a licensed person or entity, to conduct and manage in the province or territory a lottery scheme that involves betting on a race — other than a horse-race — or fight, or on a single sport event or athletic contest.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>
    <ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>&lt;div&gt;Le Service d'information et de recherche parlementaires de la Bibliothèque du Parlement rédige actuellement le résumé législatif de ce projet de loi.  Entre-temps, le Service met à votre disposition le sommaire suivant.  &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Le 26 novembre 2020, le Ministre de la Justice a déposé le projet de loi C-13, Loi modifiant le Code criminel (paris sur des épreuves sportives), à la Chambre des communes en première lecture.  &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Le projet de loi C-13 modifie l'alinéa 207(4)b) du Code criminel afin de légaliser la mise sur pied et l'exploitation dans une province ou un territoire, par le gouvernement de cette province ou de ce territoire ou par une personne ou une entité titulaire d'une licence, d'une loterie associée au pari sur une course — autre qu'une course de chevaux — ou un combat, ou une épreuve ou manifestation sportive.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>
    <ShortLegislativeSummary>&lt;div&gt;A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 26 November 2020, the Minister of Justice introduced Bill C-13, An Act to amend the Criminal Code (single event sport betting), in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.    &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-13 amends paragraph 207(4)(b) of the Criminal Code to make it lawful for the government of a province or territory, or a licensed person or entity, to conduct and manage in the province or territory a lottery scheme that involves betting on a race — other than a horse-race — or fight, or on a single sport event or athletic contest.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummary>
